<title>GREECE: GREEK FINMIN SAYS BOND TAX ISSUES TO BE CLARIFIED IN A FEW DAYS.</title>
<headline>GREEK FINMIN SAYS BOND TAX ISSUES TO BE CLARIFIED IN A FEW DAYS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek Deputy Finance Minister Nikos Christodoulakis told reporters that issues related to the taxation of government securities will be clarified in a few days.</p>
<p>The saga of tax clarification has been around since January when Greece slapped a withholding tax of 7.5 percent tax on interest income from government securities. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
